<h1>knight's tour</h1>
<p>
(classic problem)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A series of moves of a chess knight that visits all squares on the board exactly once.
</p>

<p>
<strong>See also</strong>
<a href="hamiltonianCycle.html"><em>Hamiltonian cycle</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
The associated problem is to find such a series of moves.  The problem can be generalized to an n &times; m rectangular chess board. Solutions may be found using <a href="backtrack.html"><em>backtracking</em></a>.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>
<h2>Implementation</h2>
Oleg Kiselyov's <a href="https://okmij.org/ftp/Prolog/Knight.prl" target="_blank">derivation (Prolog)</a>

<hr>

Go to the
<a href="https://www.nist.gov/dads/">Dictionary of Algorithms and Data
Structures</a> home page.

